Z||000000||btoth||03-28-2001||03:21 PM||||Well, it started happening after I replaced my dew strips.  After I reassembled the passenger side door I noticed (it's hard not to) that the windows was squeeling really bad, but only while it was going up (at about the half-way point).  So, i figured that I must have tightend those little pads on the inside of the door too tight for the window to move properly, so I loosened them up and made sure that they where put right were the outline had been made by the bolts after many years, but didn't tighten them very tight at all.  While I was in ther I also made sure the track was lubed up good.  Well, today it started again, but now it happens while the window is going down, too.  Does anyone have any suggestions about what it could be?  (I have power windows if that makes a difference.)||||reg||5
Z||000001||Greg Piet||03-28-2001||08:13 PM||||I had teh same problem, but I could slightly adjust those pads...  I also did not tighten them down real hard and mine has been quiet...<BR>no more useful input from me...   sorry<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||03-29-2001||11:28 AM||||It may be just the fact that your dewstrips are brand new.  Our brand new truck did the same thing, and the dealer sprayed some sort of dry (non silicone or solvent) lubricant on the strips and they have not squeaked since.<P><P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
